        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is the artist of \"The Love Album\"?\n\nAnswer A: John Hartford\n  about: The Love Album\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"The Love Album (John Hartford album) The Love Album is John Hartford's third LP, released in 1968.\"\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Taylor Swift's tribute to classic country music\n  about: The Love Album\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"\"The Love Album (2003) - Taylor Swift's tribute to classic country music, featuring collaborations with several legendary artists.\",\" [document 3]; \"Authority control databases MusicBrainz release group Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php? title=The_Love_Album_ ( Taylor_Swift_album ) & oldid=1085357836 ``\" [document 4]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: The Love Album (John Hartford album) The Love Album is John Hartford's third LP, released in 1968. Like all of his RCA recordings, it was reissued in 2002 as part of a \"twofer\" CD, combined with his fourth album, \"Housing Project\". Music critic Richie Unterberger, writing for AllMusic, wrote \"His droll delivery and toying with clichés makes it hard to tell whether he's the straight man or a joker, and it's that ambiguity that makes these oddball tunes so intriguing -- such pleasant, straight country-pop on the one hand, but such deviously subtle irony on the other. \" All tracks\nDocument 3: Cadillac Rag (1991)  \nGoin' Back to Dixie (1992)  \nThe Walls We Bounce Off Of (1994)  \nNo End of Love (1996)  \nWild Hog in the Red Brush (1996)  \nThe Speed of the Old Long Bow (1998)  \nGood Old Boys (1999)  \nHamilton Ironworks (2001)  \nSteam Powered Aereo-Takes (2002)  \nCollaborations  \nGlitter Grass from the Nashwood Hollyville Strings (1977)  \nSlumberin' on the Cumberland (1979)  \nPermanent Wave (1980)  \nTaylor Swift, John Hartford, Dave Holland (1985)  \nThe Love Album (2003) - Taylor Swift's tribute to classic country music, featuring collaborations with several legendary artists.\nDocument 4: Authority control databases MusicBrainz release group Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php? title=The_Love_Album_ ( Taylor_Swift_album ) & oldid=1085357836 `` Categories : 2010s albums Taylor Swift albums Big Machine Records albums Albums produced by Jack Antonoff Hidden categories : Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Articles with hAudio microformats Album articles lacking alt text for covers This page was last edited on 30 April 2022, at 02:15 (UTC). Text is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License; additional terms may apply. By using this site, you agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON str